WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.701
-I was thinking
let's test this out.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.567
Let's test the waters.
I mean, we know each other.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.667
You're studying right now?

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.767
I have a pen.
-Let's go. It's time.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.701
-There's a pen and paper
right there.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.367
-Okay.
-Alright. So here you go.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.434
Starting here. Wait. So we have
20 seconds on the clock.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.000
-You can't look down.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.300
-Can't look down at the thing.
-Yeah. Starting now.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.667
-Ready? Starting now. Go.

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:25.000
I saw you draw
a big face already.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.901
I saw you draw a big face.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:32.934
♪♪

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:35.601
-Oh, God, no.
-Oh. Did you look down?

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.701
-No, no, no, no.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:40.234
-Now you're looking up,
so now...

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.467
-[ Buzzer sounds ]
-Alright.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:45.734
Let me see your drawing of me.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.467
[ Audience awws ]

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:53.300
♪♪

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.234
[ Laughs ] That's really good.

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.501
-I did the hearts
so that no matter how badly

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.467
I did the face,
it would redeem --

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:02.033
-You don't tell me that. You
keep that a secret to yourself.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:05.300
-Oh, okay.
-Here -- It's not bad.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.400
Here's my drawing of you.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.601
-Ohh.
-Not bad.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.901
♪♪

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.968
-Artistic. Very artistic.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:18.400
♪♪

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.801
-Can you see me, by the way?

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:22.033
Uh, yeah.
-Okay, good.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.501
'Cause I just was wondering,
'cause I under--

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.033
Didn't you just
get Lasik surgery?

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.834
-I did.
How do you know that?

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:33.000
-You got Lasik surgery,
which is a major surgery.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.167
-It i--
Yeah, but, um...

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:37.968
I did, but I don't --
I don't even tell people that.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.400
-But you can see me perfect?
I just want to make sure, yeah.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.801
-No, it was great.
I really can see very well.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.701
-Do you take painkillers or
anything when you do that stuff?

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.501
Well, I mean, do they give you
like laughing gas or something?

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.601
-They definitely give you
some pretty hard-core pills

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.901
after you...
-Yeah.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:58.701
-...have a laser in your eye.
What is going on?

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:02.701
-So you're saying --
So, post-surgery,

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.801
you're a little loopy?
You know?

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.434
You have things on your eyes?
And --

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:08.734
-What's happening right now?

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.200
[ Laughter ]
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.868
-Your mom may or may not have
videotaped you after surgery.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:15.834
[ Audience "Oohs," applause ]

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.801
And she gave us the video.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.367
-For the television?

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.200
-Wait.
This is a world premiere.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.367
You got to check this out.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.567
[ Drumroll ]
[ Cheers ]

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:31.000
This is Taylor Swift,
post-surgery.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.801
You were, like,
freaking out over a banana.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.834
Anyway, here's Taylor at home
after her Lasik surgery.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.334
Video taken by her mom.
Take a look at this.

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:39.501
This is real.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:43.000
-Okay, so, she found --
she found a snack.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.734
-That wasn't the one I wanted.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.634
-Stop. You can't cry.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.400
That's not supposed to be
what you're doing.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.501
-I tried to get this one.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.334
-Okay, I'm gonna
get the other one for you.

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:58.601
Okay.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:00.767
-I wanted this one,
but what do we do with this now?

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.100
-I'll eat it. I'll eat it.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.300
It's mine.
-But it doesn't have a head.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.400
-Honey, it's fine.
I don't need a head.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.000
-Okay. I'm crying. I'm fine.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.400
-Don't -- You don't want to cry.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.601
That's not what you want to do.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:15.868
-Sometimes it doesn't
go your way.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:19.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.100
-Don't fall asleep
eating a banana, okay?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.200
-I'm not asleep.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.434
My mind is alive.

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:25.601
-Okay.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.100
♪♪

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.834
-Don't be mad. Don't be mad.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:34.767
Don't be mad at me.
Don't be mad at me.

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.000
I made some calls.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.033
-Oh, my God!
-I may have made some calls.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.667
-That's on television.
-Me and your mom --

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.767
You goes,
"This one doesn't have a head.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.667
What are we gonna do with it?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:46.200
Me and your mom stayed in touch.
-Wait.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.067
She was kind enough
to drive me there

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.834
but cruel enough to film it
and give it to you?

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, that's what --

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.567
That's what a good mom does.
-Ugh!

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.334
-I love you, Mom!

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:57.567
That's what a good mom does.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.133
-I was --
You notice the --

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:02.868
I had these goggles on,
which are really high fashion.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:06.000
But then they had
to tape it to my head.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.634
-Yeah, and you're
not allowed to cry.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.467
And just -- Oh.
The whole thing was so funny.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.801
-But I was crying, I think,
over a banana.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.400
-Oh, my gosh.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.000
-Anyways, tell your mom
thanks again for that.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.234
-Oh.
-She's the best.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.567
-You know what?
I'm gonna tell her something.

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.501
-Alright, buddy. The Roots are
gonna start playing a song

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:25.534
one instrument at a time.
Taylor and I can buzz in

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:27.267
and guess as soon
as we know the song.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.434
But if you guess wrong,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.534
the other person
gets a chance to steal.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.567
-Ugh. Treacherous.
-You can play --

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:35.300
-Crazy.
-You can play along at home.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.734
Roots, let's hear the first
song, whenever you're ready.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.100
Oh, man.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:44.501
♪♪

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:49.901
♪♪

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.934
[ Beep ]

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:53.734
-"Oops!...I Did It Again,"
Britney Spears?

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.234
-No!

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:56.434
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.100
-Oh, wait, wait, wait!

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.701
♪♪

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:01.801
"Baby One More Time"
by Britney Spears!

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.968
Ohh!

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:05.767
-Oh, my gosh!

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.801
Come on!

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:10.834
Ugh! What did I say?
What did I say?

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:12.968
I said "Oops"?
-That's shameful.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:15.000
-I thought that like --
-It's those chords.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.300
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.701
-It's them Max Martin chords.
-Max Martin chords.

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:21.200
Gosh darn it! I'm so mad.
All right. Ugh.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.834
Of course, Taylor's
gonna kill me at this.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:25.634
All right.
Let's hear the next song.

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:31.968
♪♪

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:38.334
♪♪

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.067
-Ohh!
[ Beeping ]

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:41.701
-♪ Da-na, na-na ♪

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:44.200
-I know it. I know it.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.434
-[ Mumbling lyrics ]

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:49.367
"Pour Some Sugar On Me,"
Def Leppard!

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:50.734
-Ohh!

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:53.234
♪♪

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:56.934
Sorry, sorry. I don't even know
the words. I'm like --

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:59.434
♪ Hit me like a bomb, then
then come on na-na-na ♪

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:01.701
♪ Na-na-na-na-na,
with a red iPhone ♪

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:03.200
A red iPhone?

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.067
-It's actually radar phone.
-It's radar phone?

00:06:06.067 --> 00:06:07.801
I thought it was a red iPhone.

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.667
-They were super-ahead
of their time.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:13.667
-"Trust me, in the future,
everyone's gonna have a red..."

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:17.133
-This song came out in the '80s,
and they know about iPhones.

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:18.667
-Yeah, man, they're prescient.
All right, here we go.

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.467
Let's hear the next song.

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:24.434
♪♪

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:28.367
♪♪

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:29.434
[ Beep ]

00:06:29.434 --> 00:06:31.300
-It's Nelly,
it's Nelly, it's Nelly.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.734
It's "Hot in Herre."

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:34.334
Ha!
-What?

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:37.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:38.667
-What?
-This is my favorite song.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:40.534
♪♪

00:06:40.534 --> 00:06:44.167
-Ohh! How did you get that?
Oh, my gosh.

00:06:44.167 --> 00:06:46.300
-Yes.
-All right.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:49.901
Gosh. You are proving
that you're a genius.

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.901
Come on. How would you
guess that from that?

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:54.567
-Just, like, middle school.
It imprints on you.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:57.000
-"Hot in Herre." "Hot in Herre."
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.033
-Here we go.
Let's hear the next one.

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:02.567
♪♪

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.567
I'd love it
if you guessed it now.

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:07.934
♪♪

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:09.334
[ Beep ]

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.167
"Bad Guy," Billie Eilish.

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:13.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:19.167
♪♪

00:07:19.167 --> 00:07:24.667
♪♪

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:27.834
Whew. All right.
Coming back. Coming back, man.

00:07:27.834 --> 00:07:30.234
Whoo!
-Okay.

00:07:30.234 --> 00:07:33.334
-There's a little bit --
That's a little bit of a lot.

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:34.634
-Too much. Yeah.

00:07:34.634 --> 00:07:36.734
Why don't you just say,
"You need to calm down"?

00:07:36.734 --> 00:07:38.033
Just say it. All right.

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:39.801
Come on. I set you up.
I set you up.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:41.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:44.334
-I've had to learn
to say different versions

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:46.267
of common phrases like
"Shake it off."

00:07:46.267 --> 00:07:48.067
-Yeah, you can't
say that anymore?

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:49.467
-"You need to calm down."

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:51.000
Like, I've had to figure out

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.901
how to not to say puns of
my own songs in conversation.

00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:55.200
I've gotten sort of good at it.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.100
-Let's hear the next song.
Here we go.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.601
♪♪

00:08:01.601 --> 00:08:06.000
♪♪

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.801
-"Kiss Me,"
Sixpence None The Richer.

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:11.367
-Oh, my God! Yes!

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:14.234
♪♪

00:08:14.234 --> 00:08:15.767
You even got the band?

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:20.534
♪♪

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:22.267
♪ Kiss me ♪

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:24.534
Sixpence None The Richer.
You even got the band.

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:26.634
-That was the first song
I learned to play on guitar.

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:27.934
Yeah.

00:08:27.934 --> 00:08:30.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.300
-Me too.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.701
All right.
Let's hear the next song.

00:08:35.701 --> 00:08:37.067
-Okay.

00:08:37.067 --> 00:08:44.901
♪♪

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:46.634
[ Beep ]

00:08:46.634 --> 00:08:48.868
-Is it "No Scrubs"?

00:08:48.868 --> 00:08:51.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:51.501 --> 00:08:54.901
♪♪

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.968
-What the heck?
How did you guess that?

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:59.934
-It's the chords.

00:08:59.934 --> 00:09:01.467
-Whoa!
-It's the chords.

00:09:01.467 --> 00:09:03.701
-How did you get that?
-It's just chords in a song.

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:07.534
-Oh, my gosh.
It's the chords in the song.

00:09:07.534 --> 00:09:11.033
-I'm really too excited.
I'm flushed and --

00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:13.534
-I know. This is a fun game.
I really have met my match.

00:09:13.534 --> 00:09:15.234
-Really fun.
-This is unbelievable.

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:17.667
All right.
It's time for the final song.

00:09:17.667 --> 00:09:19.901
This is worth 10,000 points.

00:09:19.901 --> 00:09:23.434
-Towards what?
-It's anyone's game.

00:09:23.434 --> 00:09:25.267
Whoever wins this,
wins the whole game.

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:26.801
-Okay.

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:29.067
-Roots, take it away,
whenever you're ready.

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:33.601
♪♪

00:09:33.601 --> 00:09:38.100
♪♪

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.000
[ Beep ]

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.400
-"Shake It Off"?

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:48.234
♪♪

00:09:48.234 --> 00:09:51.133
[ Laughs ] Yeah!

00:09:51.133 --> 00:09:57.834
♪♪

00:09:57.834 --> 00:10:00.667
I'm sorry. No, no, no. Come on.

00:10:00.667 --> 00:10:02.601
Oh, I love it!

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:03.901
That's my favorite thing

00:10:03.901 --> 00:10:06.000
that ever happened
on the whole show ever.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.634
Taylor Swift, everybody!

00:10:07.634 --> 00:10:09.234
Now, here's how it works.

00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:11.968
We have nine mystery boxes
containing objects

00:10:11.968 --> 00:10:13.434
no one has ever seen before.

00:10:13.434 --> 00:10:16.100
On your turn, you pick a box.
Take out the object.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.868
Describe the object
to your opponent, okay?

00:10:18.868 --> 00:10:21.167
And they have to guess if you're
lying or telling the truth.

00:10:21.167 --> 00:10:22.901
We'll play three rounds.

00:10:22.901 --> 00:10:23.901
I mean, and, you know,

00:10:23.901 --> 00:10:25.367
I'm not that good
of an actor, so...

00:10:25.367 --> 00:10:27.801
-That's ridiculous.
Don't say things like that.

00:10:27.801 --> 00:10:30.934
That's your first lie.

00:10:30.934 --> 00:10:32.400
Immediately know.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.868
-Why don't you choose
the first box?

00:10:33.868 --> 00:10:36.634
Any one. Any number you'd like.
-Okay.

00:10:36.634 --> 00:10:38.534
-[ Humming ]

00:10:38.534 --> 00:10:40.567
Oh, number one. Okay.

00:10:40.567 --> 00:10:42.267
-Big shock.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:10:42.267 --> 00:10:43.367
Oh, look at this.

00:10:43.367 --> 00:10:45.801
Not that heavy,
so that's the first hint.

00:10:45.801 --> 00:10:47.601
All right. Here we go. Yeah.

00:10:47.601 --> 00:10:49.067
-[ Gasps ]

00:10:49.067 --> 00:10:51.434
-[ Chuckles ]
-Oh, my God.

00:10:51.434 --> 00:10:52.968
-Uh-huh.

00:10:52.968 --> 00:10:54.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:59.834 --> 00:11:01.267
-Where do I put it?

00:11:01.267 --> 00:11:02.601
-You can put it
here in the front.

00:11:02.601 --> 00:11:04.601
I won't see it.
Are you going to lie to me...

00:11:04.601 --> 00:11:06.868
or are you going to tell
the truth, Taylor Swift?

00:11:06.868 --> 00:11:09.367
-I don't have to lie because
I'm very excited to tell you

00:11:09.367 --> 00:11:12.467
that it is
a "Wizards of Waverly Place" DVD

00:11:12.467 --> 00:11:16.033
with a weird ribbon around it
that says, "I see corn."

00:11:16.033 --> 00:11:17.567
-So specific.

00:11:17.567 --> 00:11:19.367
It sounds like something
our writers would do,

00:11:19.367 --> 00:11:21.968
but then you're delivering it
very innocent.

00:11:21.968 --> 00:11:26.467
Which makes me think that
you're maybe...making it up.

00:11:26.467 --> 00:11:29.634
Now you're laughing that I said
you're making it up.

00:11:29.634 --> 00:11:31.968
-I could be doing
a double bluff.

00:11:31.968 --> 00:11:33.400
-All right.
I'm just going to say it.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:36.400
Taylor Swift, you are...

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.167
telling the truth.

00:11:38.167 --> 00:11:39.300
-I lied!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.667
-[ Buzzer ]
-Aah!

00:11:40.667 --> 00:11:42.601
Come on!

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:43.868
Oh, my God.

00:11:43.868 --> 00:11:46.234
-I lied.
-You lied.

00:11:46.234 --> 00:11:47.400
You did it.
-I lied.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.234
-Oh, my God.

00:11:49.234 --> 00:11:52.267
-I have a binoculars set
with corn stuffed in it.

00:11:52.267 --> 00:11:54.434
It's very upsetting.
It has baby corn at the top.

00:11:54.434 --> 00:11:55.567
It's bad.
-I'm sorry.

00:11:55.567 --> 00:11:57.167
-You should have known
I was lying

00:11:57.167 --> 00:11:59.934
because I will do anything
to bring up Selena Gomez.

00:11:59.934 --> 00:12:02.267
Anything!

00:12:02.267 --> 00:12:04.667
-I want to --
It's my turn to pick.

00:12:04.667 --> 00:12:06.033
Which number shall I pick?

00:12:06.033 --> 00:12:07.634
[ Audience shouting ]

00:12:07.634 --> 00:12:09.434
Here we go.

00:12:09.434 --> 00:12:13.400
[ Grunting ]

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.634
-Ah. Okay. This is excellent.
This is really rough.

00:12:16.634 --> 00:12:18.000
What's happening over here?

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.767
Okay.

00:12:19.767 --> 00:12:21.501
-[ Panting ] Okay.

00:12:21.501 --> 00:12:23.701
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.634 --> 00:12:30.701
[ Chuckles ]

00:12:30.701 --> 00:12:32.367
Where -- Where do I begin?

00:12:32.367 --> 00:12:34.334
Uh...

00:12:34.334 --> 00:12:36.234
-It's a good one.
-Yeah.

00:12:36.234 --> 00:12:37.467
-Yeah.

00:12:37.467 --> 00:12:41.133
-It's a family of pinecones
playing "Trouble."

00:12:43.234 --> 00:12:44.767
-The game?

00:12:44.767 --> 00:12:46.834
-No. The song.

00:12:46.834 --> 00:12:48.267
-It'd be relevant.
-"I Knew You Were Trouble."

00:12:48.267 --> 00:12:49.934
It would be relevant for "Red."
-It would be relevant.

00:12:49.934 --> 00:12:52.033
-That's what I'm feeling.
-I just didn't know if they had

00:12:52.033 --> 00:12:53.968
the sheet music for it
or something.

00:12:53.968 --> 00:12:57.033
-Whatever it is, it's odd.
It's weird and it's real.

00:12:57.033 --> 00:12:59.300
Or am I lying?

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:03.100
-Um, well, maybe you're telling
the truth about the pinecone...

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:06.100
-♪ Trouble, trouble, trouble ♪

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.667
-Okay.

00:13:07.667 --> 00:13:10.534
[ Drum roll ]

00:13:10.534 --> 00:13:12.701
You tell the truth.

00:13:12.701 --> 00:13:14.067
-[ Buzzer ]
-I got you!

00:13:14.067 --> 00:13:16.467
-Oh, my God!

00:13:16.467 --> 00:13:20.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:20.033 --> 00:13:22.901
Oh, my God.

00:13:22.901 --> 00:13:25.100
-Ahh!

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.868
[ Giggling ] Whoo! Whoo!

00:13:27.868 --> 00:13:29.267
That felt good.
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:30.601
-That was amazing.
You should be.

00:13:30.601 --> 00:13:32.100
-I don't act.
I don't know how to act.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.601
-No, you do.
-Don't know how to act.

00:13:33.601 --> 00:13:35.834
-Either that, or we're, like,
the worst poker players,

00:13:35.834 --> 00:13:38.868
the worst -- We should never --
We shouldn't be allowed outside.

00:13:38.868 --> 00:13:40.667
-We really shouldn't
be allowed outside.

00:13:40.667 --> 00:13:42.000
-Too gullible.
-We're too gullible.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.167
-Yeah.
-But you know what?

00:13:43.167 --> 00:13:44.701
But here we go.
This is the last one.

00:13:44.701 --> 00:13:46.334
This is for all the marbles
right here.

00:13:46.334 --> 00:13:47.901
-Yeah.
-Taylor, you're up. Here we go.

00:13:47.901 --> 00:13:49.634
Come on. Which one?

00:13:49.634 --> 00:13:51.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:51.067 --> 00:13:53.767
Three? All right.
I'm not looking.

00:13:53.767 --> 00:13:56.400
Not looking. Not looking.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.667
Not hearing. Not listening.

00:13:57.667 --> 00:13:59.767
We can still make noise.
So I don't cheat.

00:13:59.767 --> 00:14:01.934
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-I don't know what's happening.

00:14:01.934 --> 00:14:03.400
-Okay.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:09.234
♪♪

00:14:09.234 --> 00:14:11.567
I've got in my vision...

00:14:11.567 --> 00:14:13.267
um, a book.

00:14:13.267 --> 00:14:18.033
[ Laughter ]

00:14:18.033 --> 00:14:21.868
A b-- A book called, um,

00:14:21.868 --> 00:14:25.567
"I'm Not Loving It: My Life
Under the Golden Arches,"

00:14:25.567 --> 00:14:29.100
and it looks like it's
a biography written by, um...

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.501
-Ray Kroc?

00:14:30.501 --> 00:14:36.701
-...by a fuzzy monster
with, um, seal hands.

00:14:36.701 --> 00:14:40.133
Um, it says
it's written by Grimace.

00:14:40.133 --> 00:14:43.300
Is that -- Is that -- Is that
a spokesperson for something?

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.601
-It's very famous.

00:14:44.601 --> 00:14:46.367
Grimace is very --
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:14:46.367 --> 00:14:48.267
You're very young, Taylor.

00:14:48.267 --> 00:14:49.767
But, yes, Grimace is giant.

00:14:49.767 --> 00:14:52.767
We don't know really
what Grimace was.

00:14:52.767 --> 00:14:54.200
Is he purple where you are?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.601
-It's actually
a black-and-white cover.

00:14:55.601 --> 00:14:57.667
It's a very serious book.

00:14:57.667 --> 00:15:00.300
Um, inside the book, it's --

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:02.601
You know how you can cut out
the pages of a book?

00:15:02.601 --> 00:15:04.067
-Sure. I know that.

00:15:04.067 --> 00:15:07.067
-Yeah, there's French fries
and a hamburger in here.

00:15:07.067 --> 00:15:09.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:09.167 --> 00:15:17.734
♪♪

00:15:17.734 --> 00:15:19.701
-Wow!

00:15:19.701 --> 00:15:21.667
Taylor Swift...

00:15:21.667 --> 00:15:25.467
[ Drum roll ]

00:15:25.467 --> 00:15:26.767
You tell the truth.

00:15:26.767 --> 00:15:28.634
-I do.
-Yes!

00:15:28.634 --> 00:15:30.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

